      {
        "id": 146373,
        "name": "bluedarky",
        "username": "bluedarky",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/{size}/1975_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-08-19T19:03:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"metlarcturus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/metlarcturus/48/2210_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> metlarcturus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>dpt wrote:</b><br><blockquote>For independent story reasons, it would also be very, very odd to Dana to become Galactra. Dana Bertrand and Meredith Simpson are protrayed as a happy couple, and that kind of twist just doesn't make sense to me.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;\n<p>Lasting relationships are extremely rare in comic books. Even relationships that do last are plagued by misfortune and unfortunate twists. Part of it is writers looking for plot points, but think of what it would be like to be in a relationship with a superhero. Tough.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wouldn't work with Tachyon, Dana probably has at least one piece of jewelry with a tracking device on and Meredith is the fastest woman alive. &nbsp;I can imagine the threatening phonecall now.</p>\n<p>\"Alright Tachyon, we have your girl, now bring the… GAHHH! What the hell!? MY LEGS, YOU BROKE MY FREAKING LEGS YOU SUPERSONIC FREAK! No, I'm sorry, I'll never go near her again I promise, please don't hurt me any more…\"</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:24:18.305Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
